# Files the generator must NOT write, and why. Same syntax as .gitignore.
#
# The document is generated from a Spring backend, and a few of its schemas describe the
# framework rather than the API. Generating them produces types that are strictly worse than
# the ones this app already has — and worse in a way that is invisible until runtime.

# Spring's RFC 7807 model, whose fields the document declares without types: every property
# comes out `@Contextual kotlin.Any?`, which compiles and then throws when it is decoded.
# `core:network` carries the typed one the app actually reads — with the stable `code`, the
# `correlationId` and the `fieldErrors` array the generated model does not describe at all
# (REQ-API-004). Two types with the same name, one of them unusable, is worse than one.
**/ProblemDetail.kt

# The GDPR self-export (`GET /api/v1/users/me/export`): each section's `rows` is an array of
# free-form objects, which the generator can only render as `Any?` — and kotlinx.serialization
# refuses to compile that without a contextual serializer. The app does not offer the export (it is
# a web feature), so neither model is generated. Consuming it one day means a typed row model here
# first, not a serializer for `Any`. Added 2026-09-22 with the contract refresh from basetool#1999.
**/DataExport.kt
**/ExportSection.kt
